# Cursor orchestration override

Use this file only when the runtime explicitly identifies itself as Cursor;
otherwise use `docs/agent-default.md`.

- `docs/agent-contract.md` and business/research rules have priority.
- Search narrowly, make small isolated edits, and run focused tests plus
  static checks for changed instruction files.
- Treat a workflow as the unit of orchestration. Do not decompose provider or
  data tasks when Python already manages their concurrency; prevent
  `Agent × workflow × provider` amplification.
- Preserve unrelated working-tree changes. Do not reset, restore, stash, clean,
  rebase, or auto-format out-of-scope files.

This override may change search, edit, context, worktree, and test scheduling
only. It never changes domain semantics, validation gates, provider contracts,
canonical truth, or output contracts.
